+## Versioned records and legacy compatibility
 
-QR image parsing is a CLI adapter, separate from the reusable MnemoCode engine. An application that already has a QR or PDF417 scanner can pass its decoded text directly to the corresponding Unicode or color decoder instead of including a second scanner.
+Only a text file explicitly requested with `--output PATH` uses `MNC1:<mode>:<format>:<payload>`. This public prefix prevents a future recovery session from having to remember whether the file used `direct`, checksum-valid `seedshift`, exact `seedshift-legacy`, or the lossy `seedshift-legacy-valid` replacement profile; it also identifies the representation and container revision. Dates remain separate because they are the Seedshift secret or memorized input. If explicit `--mode` or `--format` flags contradict a versioned record, MnemoCode stops instead of silently using the wrong decoder. QR images deliberately contain only the raw representation and never this descriptive header.
 
-The export engine exposes a versioned `colorCardTemplates` registry for a future graphical template picker. All seven templates are compact A6 landscape cards designed as one contemporary editorial series: a Swiss-style studio index, *Travel-Inspired Shades*, *Bold Tones for Bright Ideas*, *Modern Shades for Meaningful Work*, *Palette Notes for Creative Minds*, *Thoughtful Tones for Modern Living*, and *Glossy Material Study*. Template 2 accepts a custom `--title`; its default is *Travel-Inspired Shades*. Every supported BIP39 length fits on one card, with swatch dimensions adapting to the number of encoded colors. Template 4 places the complete color set beside an original contemporary-architecture image and repeats the exact codes in a compact material index. Template 7 uses the dedicated travertine-interior design: it retains the hue of each encoded RGB value while moderating extreme brightness and saturation for its lacquered material rendering. The ordinary exact `#RRGGBB` code is printed beneath every sample and the QR retains the unchanged standard HEX payload, so the visual finish never participates in decoding. Templates that reorder swatches visually use the embedded ordering information in each color code; display order therefore does not affect decoding.
+Existing files, pasted strings, and QR codes without a header remain supported. Supply their original `--mode` and `--format` exactly as before.
