+## SSKR threshold shares
+
+`encode --sskr`, `sskr-combine`, and `sskr-export` support N-of-M SSKR, including 2-of-3. Choose one QR card per share, an A6/A4 color collection per share, or separate numbered color cards forming each share. Existing card profiles are supported. See [SSKR commands, formats and recovery](docs/SSKR.md).
+
+SSKR is an optional output stage: `encode --sskr --threshold 2 --shares 3`.
+`--format` still selects the encoded mnemonic display; `--share-format ur|colors`
+selects the share display. `--pdf` collects every share into one PDF, while
+`--cards-dir` creates separate member files. Both may be requested together.
+`sskr-split` remains available as a compatibility alias.
+
+## Current template and export matrix
+
+All sixteen templates support `--page-size a4|a6|wallet|business`, portrait/landscape,
+collection PDF output and individual `--cards-dir` files. Wallet means 85.6 x 54 mm;
+business means 90 x 50 mm. Business collections default to A6; material selections
+default to wallet size. When `--card-qr` is enabled, small business collections and material selections use the
+reverse for their QR. Individual fragments contain only their own reference and no
+whole-collection QR. All fragments of an ordinary representation are required. For SSKR, the full
+member folder reconstructs one share; then the configured threshold of shares is required.
+
+| ID | Design |
+| --- | --- |
+| business-architect | Architecture |
+| business-it | IT |
+| business-estate | Property consultant |
+| business-diagonal | City photograph with diagonal accent |
+| business-contact | Light contact blocks |
+| business-curves | Layered dark curves |
+| business-facets | Light geometric corners |
+| business-mixed | One identity across the seven business designs |
+| material-vehicle | Matte and satin vehicle wrap finishes |
+| material-enclosure | Anodised enclosure finishes |
+| material-tile | Bathroom tiles |
+| material-switch | Switch finishes |
+| material-kitchen | Kitchen material selection |
+| business-glass-4in1 | Frosted glass, four ordered references per card |
+| business-glass-6in1 | Compact glass, six ordered references per card |
+| business-glass-8in1 | Compact glass, eight ordered references per card |
+
+`business-mixed` also supports individual files: each reference gets the next design,
+cycling after seven. The company, name and contacts stay identical. Material headings
+use `--studio-name` for the issuing studio and `--card-name` for the recipient.
+Both receive independently selected defaults when omitted.
+Each photographic sample carries its actual finish name and the **exact** encoded Ref.
+The nearest available realistic photographic finish is selected for appearance only;
+it is not guaranteed to match the RGB value exactly and does not affect recovery.
+
+```bash
+node dist/mnemocode.js preview --all --words 24 --page-size wallet --pdf all-wallet-previews.pdf
+node dist/mnemocode.js preview --template business-mixed --page-size business --cards-dir ./mixed-cards
+node dist/mnemocode.js preview --template material-vehicle --studio-name "AURORA STUDIO" --card-name "John Smith" --pdf wrap-preview.pdf
+```
+
+### Four-, six- and eight-reference glass cards
+
+`business-glass-4in1` groups four consecutive references into each 90 x 50 mm
+card. A 12-word representation uses two cards; a 24-word representation uses
+four. The final card can contain fewer references. Reference numbers preserve
+order. QR is optional (`--card-qr`); each ordinary card QR contains ONLY that card’s references, not the
+whole phrase. Concatenate all card references in numbered order for decoding.
+With SSKR `--card-layout individual`, each member folder must remain complete;
+`--card-layout qr` stores one full member in its QR.
+
+The additional `business-glass-6in1` and `business-glass-8in1` templates group six or eight references per card. For a 24-word mnemonic (16 ordinary RGB references), they produce three or two individual cards respectively. The final group may be incomplete; no padding references are printed. SSKR uses its own transport length and groups each member separately.
+
+With `--card-qr`, compact glass variants use inline QR only when its module size fits at the actual printed dimensions. Smaller A6 collections use one reverse QR rather than shrinking individual QR codes below the layout limit. PDF and PNG/JPEG exports share these decisions.
+
+
+All templates support optional image output using the same PDF renderer:
+`--images-dir NEW_FOLDER` exports collection pages as PNG by default;
+`--image-format jpg` selects JPEG. For separate cards use `--cards-dir NEW_FOLDER
+--image-format png`. Images are rendered locally at 300 dpi by the optional
+Poppler `pdftoppm` executable. No new npm dependency or online service is used.
+PDF export does not require Poppler. PNG preserves text and QR edges losslessly;
+JPEG uses quality 90. Physical translucency is simulated by the fixed glass artwork.
+
+### Collection-sheet identity
+
+The design studio on a collection sheet is independent of the employer inside its business cards. One studio is selected from 37 deduplicated names, with independent choices from 30 print slogans, five subtitles and six footers. The selection is reused throughout one export, including all SSKR members and simultaneously saved formats. A separate identity selection chooses one employer, compatible role and Latin-script full name; automatic email and website labels follow that employer.
+
+Use `--studio-name "Alder & Vale"` for the sheet studio and `--card-company "Your Company"` for the employer. `--card-slogan`, `--card-subtitle`, `--card-footer`, and `--card-reference-label` override optional copy; `-` hides an optional field. Omitted personal fields use the independently selected card identity described above.
+
+QR is disabled on ordinary cards by default; add `--card-qr` when wanted. SSKR export defaults to `--card-layout collection` without QR; explicit `--card-layout qr` enables the complete-member QR. Individual SSKR fragments never receive a full-member QR; with `--card-qr`, only their own printed references are encoded.
+
